<title>UK: TENNIS-KRAJICEK BEATEN AT WIMBLEDON BY HENMAN.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-KRAJICEK BEATEN AT WIMBLEDON BY HENMAN.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-07-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Wimbledon champion Richard Krajicek of the Netherlands lost his men's singles title on Wednesday when he was beaten in the fourth round by Tim Henman. The 14th seeded Briton won 7-6 (9-7) 6-7 (7-9)_7-6 (7-5) 6-4.</p>
</text>
